---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/docs/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/docs/Callout.astro';
import PrevNext from '../../../components/docs/PrevNext.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="get_god_nodes">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4">get_god_nodes</h1>
  <p class="text-xl text-text-secondary mb-8">
    Find the project hotspots - the most connected nodes by semantic degree.
  </p>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">Description</h2>
    <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
      The <code class="text-primary bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-1 rounded">get_god_nodes</code> tool surfaces the "god nodes" of your codebase: the classes, interfaces, and functions with the highest semantic degree - counting incoming and outgoing <code class="text-primary bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-1 rounded">CALLS</code>, <code class="text-primary bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-1 rounded">USES</code>, <code class="text-primary bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-1 rounded">EXTENDS</code>, and <code class="text-primary bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-1 rounded">IMPLEMENTS</code> edges.
    </p>
    <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
      Incoming degree tells you where a change ripples widest (ports, providers, value objects). Outgoing degree reveals local fan-out and complexity. Degree counts raw edges (a class using a type in 3 methods counts 3), not distinct dependents - use <code class="text-primary bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-1 rounded">get_impact</code> for the precise blast radius.
    </p>
    <p class="text-text-secondary">
      Results are returned in a compact format: <code class="text-primary bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-1 rounded">degree | in/out | role | type | Name | filePath:line</code> (role: ripple/fanout/hub).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">Parameters</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm text-left text-text-secondary">
        <thead class="text-xs uppercase bg-bg-subtle text-text-muted">
          <tr>
            <th class="py-3 px-4 rounded-tl-lg">Parameter</th>
            <th class="py-3 px-4">Type</th>
            <th class="py-3 px-4">Required</th>
            <th class="py-3 px-4 rounded-tr-lg">Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="bg-bg-subtle">
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-primary"><code class="text-primary">top_n</code></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4">integer</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="text-text-muted">No</span></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4">Number of top hotspots to return: 1-100 (default: 20)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-primary"><code class="text-primary">sort_by</code></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4">string</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="text-text-muted">No</span></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4">Rank by <code class="text-xs bg-bg-subtle px-1 rounded text-primary">in</code> (incoming = ripple/blast radius, default), <code class="text-xs bg-bg-subtle px-1 rounded text-primary">out</code> (outgoing = fan-out/complexity), or <code class="text-xs bg-bg-subtle px-1 rounded text-primary">degree</code> (total)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-primary"><code class="text-primary">scope</code></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4">string</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="text-text-muted">No</span></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4"><code class="text-xs bg-bg-subtle px-1 rounded text-primary">main</code> (prod only, excludes tests, default), <code class="text-xs bg-bg-subtle px-1 rounded text-primary">test</code>, or <code class="text-xs bg-bg-subtle px-1 rounded text-primary">all</code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-border">
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-primary"><code class="text-primary">exclude_accessors</code></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4">boolean</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="text-text-muted">No</span></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4">Drop trivial accessors (getName/setX/isY backed by a real property) to de-noise getter-heavy code (default: false)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-text-primary"><code class="text-primary">project_path</code></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4">string</td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4"><span class="text-text-muted">No</span></td>
            <td class="py-3 px-4">Filter by project path. If not provided, searches all indexed projects</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">Example</h2>
    <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
      Ask Claude to reveal the system hotspots. Each line shows the degree, the in/out split, the node's role, its type, name, and location.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      code={`⏺ codegraph:get_god_nodes (MCP)(top_n: 5, sort_by: "in")

  ⎿  GOD NODES (5):
     42 | 40/2  | ripple | Interface | UserRepository | .../domain/port/UserRepository.kt:7
     31 | 28/3  | ripple | Class     | User           | .../domain/model/User.kt:7
     27 | 5/22  | fanout | Class     | AuthController | .../api/AuthController.kt:19
     24 | 12/12 | hub    | Class     | UserService    | .../application/UserService.kt:15
     19 | 17/2  | ripple | Class     | Email          | .../domain/model/Email.kt:5`}
      lang="bash"
      title="Claude Code"
      copyable={false}
    />
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-4">Use Cases</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-text-secondary">
      <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <span class="text-secondary mt-1">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span><strong class="text-text-primary">Onboarding:</strong> Quickly find the handful of types every new contributor must understand first</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <span class="text-secondary mt-1">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span><strong class="text-text-primary">Refactoring targets:</strong> High-fanout nodes are prime candidates for splitting into smaller, focused units</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <span class="text-secondary mt-1">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span><strong class="text-text-primary">Change risk:</strong> High-incoming nodes are the riskiest to modify - a single change ripples across the codebase</span>
      </li>
      <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
        <span class="text-secondary mt-1">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span><strong class="text-text-primary">Test prioritization:</strong> Focus test coverage on the most-depended-upon parts of the system</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Callout type="tip" title="Ripple vs Fan-out">
    Sort by <code class="text-primary">in</code> to find the nodes a change ripples out from (ports, value objects, base classes). Sort by <code class="text-primary">out</code> to find over-connected callers that may be doing too much. The <code class="text-primary">role</code> column labels each node ripple, fanout, or hub accordingly.
  </Callout>

  <Callout type="info" title="Degree vs Impact">
    Degree counts raw edges, not distinct dependents, so it is a fast heuristic for "where is the coupling". When you need the exact set of nodes affected by a change, follow up with <code class="text-primary">get_impact</code>.
  </Callout>

  <PrevNext
    prev={{ title: "get_file_symbols", href: "/docs/tools/get-file-symbols" }}
    next={{ title: "get_module_overview", href: "/docs/tools/get-module-overview" }}
  />
</DocsLayout>
